      ],
      "image": "assets/images/228498/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Season ribs with salt and pepper.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/f52RjCkZSNOUTprWfHjPqInOM1g=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/228498-slow-cooker-baby-back-ribs-DDMFS-002-step02-67ac3dc812414027833511ddd575fb77.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/228498/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour 1/2 cup water into the slow cooker, then add ribs. Scatter onion and garlic over top. Cover and cook on Low for 8 hours or High for 4 hours.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/WaKoqiDMEH2WcScvN4en9W2zr5o=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/228498-slow-cooker-baby-back-ribs-DDMFS-004-step04-a6df006c14f245be91de330b7e5f06a8.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/228498/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "When the ribs are almost finished, preheat the oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Transfer ribs from the slow cooker to a baking sheet; discard onion and garlic. Coat ribs with barbeque sauce.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/jLQgAPnQCCk81d1Kq5eRJDV0Lfc=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/228498-slow-cooker-baby-back-ribs-DDMFS-004-step05-90c5e41a5e02416e922be32e56d4bc1f.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/228498/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake ribs in the preheated oven until sauce caramelizes and sticks to meat, 10 to 15 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/GSnnjvadcRnBY-n2uRL7DcvlqiE=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/228498-slow-cooker-baby-back-ribs-DDMFS-004-step06-9b8e6357218541f99f2502f865d02663.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/228498/step_06.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enjoy! No need to fire up the grill or smoker to enjoy finger-licking good barbecue ribs. This slow cooker ribs recipe will quickly become your favorite set-it-and-forget-it meal. The fall-off-the bone meat is a surefire crowd-pleaser. Once the meat is perfectly tender, the sauce gets brown and bubbly thanks to a quick session in the oven. No one will know you didn't spend the whole day tending to these these delicious ribs.",
